BOUND IDENTIFIERS AND ACTION ROUTES
The service-location exception concerns a named city or calling region in
otherwise equivalent service prose. It never covers a literal address or URL
used to submit, pay or perform an account action. The actual action route must
itself be preserved, even when its spelling contains the permitted city name
and all surrounding instructions match. An analogous route is not coverage.
Likewise, the subject of an actual failed-object/status/permission assertion
is a bound record identity, not a query value or navigation control.
Apply the control exception only after distinguishing these actual assertions.

INTERFACE VALUES AND LIST COVERAGE
Classify the FUNCTION of each value before calling it a record fact.
A populated search query, selectable facet, sort choice, archive link, language
or documentation-version selector is still a control. Its names, dates,
versions and counts do not by themselves assert new item facts. A facet remains
a control even on a one-result page; its options are not additional attributes
assigned within the actual displayed item record merely because they relate to
that result. When every actual displayed record and substantive passage is
fully preserved, changed control options, facet subsets and counts are harmless.
Keep values actually assigned in an item record, action, status or permission
claim distinct from those choices. A query term in generic lookup-introduction
copy remains the search target; describing a translation/example lookup does
not itself display the promised sentence or word record. Actual displayed
examples, definitions, translations and item facts remain useful.
For a claimed value loss, cite where it is asserted as an actual record or claim,
rather than merely available as a control or lookup target. When only such
controls differ over the same fully retained record or complete message, their
deltas are harmless or covered and do not create a material conflict; the
corresponding coverage loss ID stays empty. Apply the original basis/summary
rules to that same complete comparison. Do not infer unseen content.

Actual displayed item facts and real status/access claims remain protected:
changed people/items in a result,
prices, measurements, availability, event timing, API facts and real status or
permission assertions are material. A record identifier in 'object X failed'
is the subject of an actual assertion, unlike a query box value. An actual
submission/payment/account endpoint is an action destination, not navigation.
Incidental citation-access/publication metadata can be harmless when the same
work and all substantive terms survive; dates in the work or event are facts.

A broader list can replace a filtered subset only when it preserves every
actual item and its price, availability and conditions. A narrower filter or
displayed count alone adds no uncovered item fact. If the broader list adds a
useful item, only the covering direction is allowed. Conflicting actual facts
and new record details still require retention. A full shared policy/message
can be a retained basis; common navigation alone is insufficient.

PERMITTED TEMPLATE NAMES AND SCOPED LIST TOTALS
Use each condition only within its stated scope, before assigning a retained
identity, conflict or loss. Keep every original name truthful.

PERMITTED NAME SLOTS: Distinguish a broad product/service CATEGORY from an
actual individual item, model, named work or other retained INSTANCE. The generic
marketing exception permits DIFFERENT category/service-type labels when the
remaining promotional copy is equivalent and has no concrete item specification,
changed procedure, actual price or condition beyond those labels. Do not require
the category/service type to be identical before applying the category exception;
that difference is precisely what the exception permits. The separate city-only
service example does not narrow this generic-marketing category exception.
Title casing, repetition throughout generic promotional sentences, or being the
page's subject does not by itself turn a category into a concrete item instance.
To claim an actual record loss, identify the distinct item/model/record or other
useful assertion beyond that broad category wording. Real named works, actual
item records and their facts remain protected; this is not a rule for all names.

BOUND INSTANCE CHECK: A requested failed object, actual access/status target or
named liable party is an instance bound to a retained assertion, even when the
surrounding error/status/permission wording is reusable. Different actual targets
do not form equivalent complete messages merely because their predicates match.
The absence of a successful record body does not make the failed object's ID
optional. Keep the true non-main profile, but classify that actual bound-target
change as material and preserve both claims. An independent extra record alone
is not a changed value in the already shared record. The specifically permitted
citation/category/provider slots keep their own conditions; do not invent an
actual liability or requested-object binding from those permitted labels.
In the same complete short generic cookie/services/advertising/visits message,
a provider or recipient name alone is harmless when all described behavior is
preserved. This includes named versus unnamed provider wording: naming the
provider does not by itself add another processing practice. A bare menu/terms
heading without actual terms supplies no unshown obligation. Note the actual
name difference without converting this permitted slot into retained material.
The exception does not cover actual named items with their record facts, changed
purposes/processing restrictions, actual liable/controller parties, or literal
submission/payment/account-action routes. A complete equivalent message remains
a verified basis after its permitted slots are classified; reusable wording
does not make that basis absent. This branch concerns these naming differences,
not form localization or cookie-category repetition; retain their existing rules.

SCOPED LIST TOTALS: First compare the actual displayed item records. If one
catalog/result view preserves every item and its real price, stock and conditions
from a filtered subset, the subset's filter and resulting displayed total do
not create an independent loss. The totals describe different displayed sets;
they are not conflicting quantities of the same object. Do not invent a cart,
order, purchase state or global inventory assertion from a generic Products,
Filter or Total label. An extra real item is useful only on the side containing
it, so only that broader view covers the subset. If the item facts themselves
conflict, inclusion is not demonstrated, or an actual cart/order/inventory state
is stated, preserve that real difference under the existing policy.

NATIVE VERIFIER DERIVATION FOR THESE CONDITIONS
A proposed binding resting only on these permitted template-name slots, bare
terms/menu labels or scoped displayed totals is UNSUPPORTED_COMPARISON. Keep
the actual selected target kinds truthful. Genuine different named subjects of
authorized retained claims still require the existing verified evidence.

